course: dictionary
lesson: 6110
title: Michigan, a name for a special place
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Michigan is a name, so it starts with a capital letter. It is a proper noun: the special name of one particular place. Other proper nouns include London, Scotland and Lake Michigan.
explain: Michigan is a state in the north of the United States. A state is a large region inside a country, a bit like a county inside England. Michigan is partly surrounded by the Great Lakes, which are huge lakes of water.
explain: Read the words around the name to find its meaning. «Swing states could be won by either party, so both sides pour adverts and visits into them; recent ones have included Pennsylvania, Michigan, Wisconsin, Georgia and Arizona.» The list of other states tells you that Michigan is a place, not a person or a thing.
fact: Michigan is a state in the north of the United States.
fact: Michigan is made of two peninsulas, which are pieces of land with water on three sides.
fact: Lake Michigan is one of the five Great Lakes of North America.
fact: Lake Michigan is the only Great Lake completely inside the USA.
fact: Michigan is famous for the Great Lakes, the city of Detroit and car making, and its shape is said to look like a mitten.
exercise: Michigan is written with a capital M. What kind of word is it? | A colour | A number | A verb, a doing word | *A proper noun, the special name of one place
exercise: Which of these is true about Michigan? | It is a lake in Africa | *It is a state in the north of the United States | It is a city in Japan | It is a country in Europe
exercise: «Swing states could be won by either party, so both sides pour adverts and visits into them; recent ones have included Pennsylvania, Michigan, Wisconsin, Georgia and Arizona.» In this sentence, what is Michigan? | *A place that political parties fight over | A person who sells adverts | A type of weather | A food that people eat at lunch
test: Why does Michigan start with a capital letter? | *Because it is the special name of a place | Because it is angry | Because it starts a sentence | Because it is very long
test: Lake Michigan is one of which group of lakes? | The Himalayas | The Alps | The Sahara | *The Great Lakes
exam: Which of these is the best description of Lake Michigan? | *A huge lake in North America, the only Great Lake completely inside the USA | A river in Egypt that flows into the sea | A small pond in a park | A mountain in Scotland covered in snow
